[size=5][b]VortexModLists[/b][/size]

A lightweight Windows utility to view, filter and export your Nexus Mods Vortex mod lists.

[size=4][b]Overview[/b][/size]

VortexModLists reads mod metadata directly from your local Vortex installation and displays it in an organized table. Perfect for backup, sharing, or documentation of your mod setups.

[b]No Vortex plugins needed[/b] — just point it to your Vortex data folder and go!

[size=4][b]Features[/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]Automatic Vortex Detection[/b] — Finds your mod data automatically or let you browse manually[/*]
[*][b]Multi-Game Support[/b] — Switch between all your installed games[/*]
[*][b]Smart Status Filtering[/b] — Filter by active/inactive mods directly in the table[/*]
[*][b]Multiple Export Formats[/b] — Export as CSV, Markdown, or Excel[/*]
[*][b]Quick Copy[/b] — Copy CSV/Markdown directly to clipboard[/*]
[*][b]Dark/Light Theme[/b] — Follows your Windows settings automatically[/*]
[*][b]Remembers Your Preferences[/b] — Saves window layout and column widths[/*]
[/list]

[size=4][b]Mod Details Shown[/b][/size]

For each mod, the app displays:
[list]
[*][b]Mod Name[/b] — The mod's full name[/*]
[*][b]ID[/b] — Unique mod identifier[/*]
[*][b]Version[/b] — Current mod version[/*]
[*][b]Homepage[/b] — Clickable link to the mod page[/*]
[*][b]Status[/b] — Active or Inactive indicator[/*]
[/list]

[size=4][b]Getting Started[/b][/size]

[b]Installation[/b]

1. Download the
[code]VortexModLists.zip[/code]
2. Extract it to any folder (e.g.,
[code]C:\Tools\VortexModLists[/code]
)
3. Run
[code]VortexModLists.exe[/code]

That's it! No installation, no registry changes, no dependencies to worry about.

[b]Installer + Runtime (recommended)[/b]
[list]
[*]Use [code]VortexModLists-Setup.exe[/code][/*]
[*]The installer checks for [b].NET Desktop Runtime 10 (x64)[/b] and installs it automatically if missing[/*]
[/list]

[b]Updates[/b]

For the latest version and source code, visit GitHub: [url=https://github.com/detlefs/VortexModLists]VortexModLists on GitHub[/url]
Latest Release: [url=https://github.com/detlefs/VortexModLists/releases/latest]Download here[/url]

[b]First Run[/b]

The app automatically searches for Vortex data in the standard location:
[code]C:\Users\<YourUsername>\AppData\Roaming\Vortex\temp\state_backups_full[/code]
If found, your mod list loads instantly.

[b]Manual Data Source[/b]
If automatic detection doesn't work:
1. Click [b]Browse...[/b]
2. Select either:
[list]
[*]A specific Vortex JSON file (e.g., 
[code]hourly.json[/code]
)[/*]
[*]The entire backup folder (the app searches for the newest JSON)[/*]
[/list]
3. Click [b]Search Again[/b] to reload

The app remembers your choice for next time.

[size=4][b]Exporting Your Mod Lists[/b][/size]

[b]Supported Formats[/b]
[list]
[*][b]CSV[/b] — Import into spreadsheets or databases[/*]
[*][b]Markdown[/b] — Use online, or for documentation[/*]
[*][b]Excel[/b] — Formatted 
[code].xlsx[/code]
with one sheet per game[/*]
[/list]

[b]Export Options[/b]
[list]
[*][b]Selected Game[/b] — Export only the currently viewed game[/*]
[*][b]All Games[/b] — Export mods from every managed game[/*]
[/list]

[b]Quick Actions[/b]
[list]
[*]Copy CSV to clipboard[/*]
[*]Copy Markdown to clipboard[/*]
[/list]

[size=4][b]Requirements[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Windows 10 or newer[/b] (64-bit)[/*]
[*][b]Nexus Mods Vortex[/b] installed with local state files[/*]
[/list]

[size=4][b]Vortex Data Files[/b][/size]
The app reads these Vortex JSON files (in order of preference):

1. [b]Most recent JSON[/b] in
[code]state_backups_full[/code]
folder
2.
[code]hourly.json [/code]
— Regular Vortex backup
3. 
[code]state.json [/code]
or
[code]vortex-state.json[/code]
4. Any
[code]*.json [/code]
file in the Vortex data folder

[b]Note:[/b] The app reads your Vortex data in [b]read-only mode[/b]. It never modifies your Vortex setup or deployed mods.

[size=4][b]Language Support[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]English (default)[/*]
[*]German (Deutsch)[/*]
[/list]

[size=4][b]Troubleshooting[/b][/size]
[b]"No data found"[/b]
[list]
[*]Make sure Vortex is installed and has mod data[/*]
[*]Check if 
[code]%AppData%\Vortex\temp\state_backups_full[/code]
exists[/*]
[*]Try clicking [b]Browse...[/b] and manually select the folder[/*]
[/list]

[b]App won't start[/b]
[list]
[*]Ensure you are using Windows 10 or newer[/*]
[*]Make sure .NET 10 Runtime is available (bundled with app)[/*]
[/list]

[b]Data looks outdated[/b]
[list]
[*]Click [b]Search Again[/b] to reload the latest mod data[/*]
[*]Vortex may not have created recent backups — verify in Vortex settings[/*]
[*]Restart Vortex to trigger new backups. This may be needed after adding/removing mods.[/*]
[/list]

[size=4][b]Tips & Tricks[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Use status filtering to focus on only active or inactive mods[/*]
[*]Export to Markdown for easy sharing online[/*]
[*]Export to Excel to track mod versions across your games[/*]
[*]The app remembers your custom data source path between sessions[/*]
[/list]

